This is Knobe's (2003) side-effect effect, the chairman/environment vignette. The original had a very large effect (82% vs 23%), and the effect has been replicated many times across cultures and samples. Replications of the harm/help asymmetry in intentionality judgments are robust, and the many-labs-style replication also found it. With a large effect size, a replication is very likely to reach significance even at a modest sample size.

I do recognize the study. I recall no specific failed replication of the basic effect.

