This is the Carter, Ferguson & Hassin (2011) study, "A single exposure to the American flag shifts support toward Republicanism up to 8 months later." The original had a small sample (N≈66) and p just under .05. Flag priming effects have generally failed to replicate; Many Labs 4 and related efforts found little. Klein et al. (Many Labs 2) tested the flag priming effect from Ferguson and found no effect. A direct replication of Carter et al. was also done by Klein et al. (2014) as part of Many Labs 1, which tested flag priming (Carter et al. 2011) and found no effect, with a conservatism-measure effect near zero.

The recalled outcome is therefore a failure.

